# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Punjab Pure Dairy - backend configuration template
#
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) or set these as real environment variables.
# NEVER commit a real password. NEVER hard-code one in a .cs or .json file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Targets the `dairy_farm` database.
# The database name contains spaces, which is valid for MySQL.
#
# Notes:
#   - SslMode may be omitted; the API defaults it to None for local development
#     because the local MySQL 8.4 instance has no trusted certificate.
#   - Set SslMode explicitly (Preferred/Required/VerifyCA/VerifyFull) for any
#     non-local deployment.
ConnectionStrings__DairyFarm=Server=localhost;Port=3306;Database=dairy_farm;User ID=<your-user>;Password=<your-password>;

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS - controlled origin list. Wildcards are not accepted by the API.
# Must match the origin the React frontend is served from (dev server = 3000).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=http://localhost:3000
Cors__AllowedOrigins__1=http://127.0.0.1:3000
Cors__AllowedOrigins__2=http://localhost:5173
Cors__AllowedOrigins__3=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JWT Bearer (Phase 2A)
#
# REQUIRED. The API refuses to start without these.
# The signing key MUST be at least 32 bytes.
# NEVER commit a real key. NEVER put one in appsettings.json.
#
# Generate a key with:   openssl rand -base64 48
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Jwt__Key=<generate-a-random-key-of-at-least-32-bytes>
Jwt__Issuer=PunjabPureDairy.Api
Jwt__Audience=PunjabPureDairy.Frontend
Jwt__ExpiryMinutes=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner account bootstrap (Phase 2A)
#
# Used ONLY by the explicit one-time command:
#     dotnet run -- --bootstrap-owner
#
# These are never read during normal startup, so no account is ever created
# automatically. The bootstrap refuses to run if an Owner already exists.
#
# Supply them as real environment variables or user-secrets. Never commit the
# password. Never write it into a file in this repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INITIAL_OWNER_EMAIL=owner@yourfarm.pk
# INITIAL_OWNER_PASSWORD=<at-least-12-characters-supplied-out-of-band>
# INITIAL_OWNER_NAME=Farm Owner
# FIRST-RUN ONLY. Required on a brand-new installation where the `companies`
# and `farms` tables are both empty, because users.farm_id and farms.company_id
# are NOT NULL. The bootstrap creates: company -> farm -> Owner, in one
# transaction, and is idempotent on re-run.
#
#   dotnet run -- --bootstrap-owner --with-farm "Main Dairy Farm"
#
# The farm name may be given with --with-farm "..." or here. The company name
# has no argument form and must be set here.
# INITIAL_COMPANY_NAME=<your-company-name>
# INITIAL_FARM_NAME=<your-farm-name>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
# ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5080
